Thus hierarchy: object -> candidate_root -> candidate_entity -> driver_availability_state -> origin_candidate_availability/destination_candidate_availability; and candidate_entity -> dispatch_proposal -> schedule_candidate.

Thus candidate_entity is a supertype of origin_candidate_availability, destination_candidate_availability, dispatch_proposal, schedule_candidate, etc. So create_candidate expects ?candidate - candidate_entity, which can be any of those subtypes. So we can call create_candidate on destination_availability_alpha (type destination_candidate_availability) and shift_candidate_beta (schedule_candidate). Good.

